{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JU6aasDxxsio4od7YainLf","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n001-ADJUDICATE-1e1e27c.md\nsol-review-r1.md\nsol-review-r2.md\nsol-review-r3.md\n1e1e27cb WI-838: Record Sol round 3 (01d21b26 SOUND)\n01d21b26 WI-838: IF-247 names the record file again (Sol round 2 MINOR; GPT Terra, round 3)\n6c39bcc2 WI-838: The first-mint rows cover a finished replacement and the retired-first record shape (GPT Terra, round 2)\n694:detail = \"Builds planner/critic/arbiter briefs only from SR/IF registries with strict template slots and override/fallback loading. Status, log and self-assessment data are excluded by construction; an unknown or unfilled template slot is rejected.\"\n1117:detail = \"\"\"The mechanized core of accessibility anchor A3: for every declared colour vocabulary (enumerated from the module constants, the U5/U2 closure, so a new vocabulary enters by existing), every member that actually PAINTS in a rendered document resolves to a legend swatch labelled in words in that same document, with CSS tokens resolved. Status members additionally pair a per-status glyph. The emitted JS detail-badge maps are SUBSTITUTED from TIER_FILL/STATUS_FILL rather than hand-copied, and three drift guards hold every copy equal to the constants: the emitted JS maps byte-match the Python palettes; the CSS status tokens match STATUS_FILL and are asserted theme-invariant; and the tier-legend bijection derives its expectation from the TIER_FILL dict, so a member dropped from the legend also fails. SCOPE and its narrowing: the worded cue must exist in the same document — that it sits within eyeshot of the painted element is layout this does not re-assert. The JS detail-panel badge stays out of the LEGEND rule because its background carries its concept as the badge's own visible text.\"\"\"\n1526:detail = \"\"\"The `adjudication` kind (docs/concurrency-v2.md §A5.2) joins the declared SafetyClass vocabulary: exclusive on the concurrency axis, rank 1 on the order axis - the slot §A1 reserved, filled without renumbering the ruled table. The kind's lane runs NO product bar (integrate._lane_bar_directives + _refresh_bar: the refresh still merges trunk in, runs the trunk step and commits a verified Bar-Green attestation whose summary reads no-bar honestly) because its outputs are Status cells and the work registry, nothing a product bar can speak to; a mixed batch or unreadable frontmatter fails TOWARD the bar. The optional `bar = DevStg-Reqs|DevStg-Tests|DevStg-Impl` frontmatter key rides the same directive read: bar declares verification strictness for this row's lane; it never affects scheduling (load_wis deliberately does not parse it) - the refresh passes the batch's strictest value to check.py --gate and refuses a malformed one loudly.\"\"\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2584b99b-5c67-48ab-94cc-44374d289363","uuid":"2136c814-de1b-4f07-a4b7-d60a690e8fbf","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:48:36.754Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\n001-ADJUDICATE-1e1e27c.md\nsol-review-r1.md\nsol-review-r2.md\nsol-review-r3.md\n1e1e27cb WI-838: Record Sol round 3 (01d21b26 SOUND)\n01d21b26 WI-838: IF-247 names the record file again (Sol round 2 MINOR; GPT Terra, round 3)\n6c39bcc2 WI-838: The first-mint rows cover a finished replacement and the retired-first record shape (GPT Terra, round 2)\n694:detail = \"Builds planner/critic/arbiter briefs only from SR/IF registries with strict template slots and override/fallback loading. Status, log and self-assessment data are excluded by construction; an unknown or unfilled template slot is rejected.\"\n1117:detail = \"\"\"The mechanized core of accessibility anchor A3: for every declared colour vocabulary (enumerated from the module constants, the U5/U2 closure, so a new vocabulary enters by existing), every member that actually PAINTS in a rendered document resolves to a legend swatch labelled in words in that same document, with CS