{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfmt1nDp9LwumUNxut2QX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: MEANING, 1 row (LLR-270 `Detail`). I did not re-attest it.**\n\n**Why it's MEANING:** The amendment adds new required behaviour:\n- When a route has no record, `keep_for` now writes a lease-only record before launching.\n- A lease-only record mints a new session; only an active or draining record resumes one.\n- A mint is saved only if the record still holds its own lease. Otherwise it is dropped with reset reason `store moved on`.\n- A first mint that fails removes its lease-only record, and tombstones and expired leases also handle that record.\n\nCode built correctly to the old text would fail all of this.\n\n**Why I wouldn't approve the new text:** It also drops two general rules the old text required:\n1. **The wait:** `keep_for` used to wait up to `lease_wait` on *any* lease another call held. The new text only says \"a second call meeting *that* lease waits\", which covers the first-mint lease alone.\n2. **The release:** \"keep_bookkeep and keep_abandon release it\" is gone. The new text only says they complete or remove a lease-only record.\n\nThe code still does both: `session_keep.keep_for` waits on any held lease, and `keep_bookkeep` releases it at `session_keep.py:798`. So this is a gap in the text, not a change in behaviour. But under the new wording, code that never released a resumed session's lease would no longer contradict the requirement.\n\n**What I committed (each with the `WI: WI-838` trailer):**\n- `492e5dee`: the verdict, at `docs/reviews/wi-838-first-mint-takes-a-lease/001-ADJUDICATE-1e1e27c.md`.\n- `7930e699`: a `## Dispositions` section in the WI-838 spec. It drafts one follow-up that adds both general rules back to LLR-270 `Detail` with no behaviour change, then sends the row back to adjudication. It parses cleanly with `intake.parse_dispositions`, and intake creates the work item when WI-838 merges.\n\n**Not done:**\n- I didn't run `intake.py snapshot --reattests`, so LLR-270 still differs from its approved copy until the follow-up is judged.\n- I edited no registry cells.\n\n**Outside the cells I was shown:** `code_symbol` and `test_refs` also changed on this row (new symbols such as `is_lease_only` and `store_remove`, and TC-329 added). They weren't part of this question, so I didn't judge them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":66619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2584b99b-5c67-48ab-94cc-44374d289363","uuid":"a8a693af-229f-484e-ab2e-bc81b5560edd","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:50:40.403Z","request_id":"req_011Cfmt1mVeaJ44SPo19rS4N"}
